What is a Loop in Java?
A loop is a programming statement used to execute a block of code repeatedly until a given condition becomes false.

Types of Loops in Java
1. for loop
2. while loop
3. do-while loop

1.for Loop
The for loop is used when you know how many times you want to execute a block of code.

Syntax:
for (initialization; condition; update) {
    // code to execute
}
Ex:-
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
            System.out.println(i);
        }
    }
}

2.What is a while Loop?
The while loop is used to execute a block of code repeatedly as long as the given condition is true.

Syntax
initialization;

while (condition) {
    // statements
    update;
}
Ex:-
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int i = 1;

        while (i <= 5) {
            System.out.println(i);
            i++;
        }
    }
}

3.What is a do-while Loop?
The do-while loop executes a block of code at least once, even if the condition is false.

It is an exit-controlled loop because the condition is checked after executing the loop body.

Syntax
initialization;

do {
    // statements
    update;
} while (condition);

Ex:-
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int i = 1;

        do {
            System.out.println(i);
            i++;
        } while (i <= 5);
    }
}
